# Agent artifacts (`.md` placement)

Work product **for the agent** goes in `.local/` (gitignored). Work product **for the repo** goes in `docs/`. There is no third option.

## Where a new `.md` may land

| Location | Contents |
|---|---|
| `.local/sessions/<date>_<id>_<slug>/` | Multi-request session: `REQUESTS` `TODOS` `PLAN` `MEMORY` `STATUS` — see `session-tracking.mdc` |
| `.local/tmp/<id>/` | Throwaway recon, scratch output |
| `.local/quality-backlog.md` | Gate failures (`npm run qualitygate:capture`) |
| `.local/findings/` | Scope inventories, audits, migration notes, eval writeups |
| `docs/` | **Flat allowlist only** (7 files in `scripts/structure-gates/docs-allowlist.mjs`) — no subfolders |
| `.agents/` `.cursor/` `.claude/` `.fabro/` | Prompts, rules, skills, subagent configs |
| `src/**` | Only shipped assets: `instructions.md`, `SKILL.md`, legal pages |
| Repo root | `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` only |

## Forbidden

- New `.md` at repo root — `PLAN-*.md`, `*-TRACKER.md`, `*-AUDIT.md`, `*-STATUS.md`, `*-EVAL.md`, `*-ROADMAP.md`.
- Dropping an audit or plan next to the code it describes (`scripts/USAGE-AUDIT.md`, `src/domains/<x>/NOTES.md`).
- Committing Fabro stage artifacts (`CLARIFY.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `PLAN.md`, `STRUCTURE.md`, `RETRO.md`) — they are run-local.

**Before writing any `.md`, ask: will a human read this next month?** No → `.local/`. Yes → `docs/`.

## Extend `docs/`, don't grow it

A new file in `docs/` is the **last** resort. Search first — `docs/README.md` indexes the six docs (`ARCHITECTURE`, `MODULES`, `STORYTELLER`, `DEVELOPMENT`, `MCP_API`). Agent/Mastra topics: root `AGENTS.md`.

1. Find the doc that already owns the topic and add a section to it.
2. Do **not** add a 7th file or `docs/internal/` / `docs/adr/` / etc. — expand an allowlisted file or update the allowlist + tests intentionally.
3. Never park a per-change writeup (`FOO-MIGRATION.md`, `BAR-FIX-NOTES.md`) in `docs/` — that is `.local/findings/`.

Config files are not documentation: `.env*.example`, `*.config.*`, and `package.json` get one trailing clause per line saying what the value does. Tutorials, option matrices, and worked examples go in `docs/` with the config pointing at them.

Enforced by `scripts/check-agent-artifacts.mjs` (pre-commit) and `.cursor/hooks/guard-agent-artifacts.sh` (on edit).
